      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "\"%20\" is \" \" as it is sent to a webserver, the 20 is the ascii value of the space character in octal.  Since http doesn't actually support spaces in filenames this method was developed.  The only difference is web browsers hide the %20 from you to look nice. In the spec %20 is always converted to the space character and not 20 spaces",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
